   "blocks": [
    {
     "t": "h3",
     "text": "1.1 Fundamental Concept of Combinational Circuits"
    },
    {
     "t": "p",
     "text": "A **Combinational Logic Circuit** is an interconnected network of logic gates whose digital output at any arbitrary instant $t$ is strictly and solely determined by the Boolean combination of its digital inputs applied at that identical instant $t$ (modulo the physical propagation delay of the physical gates)."
    },
    {
     "t": "p",
     "text": "Mathematically, an $m$-input, $n$-output combinational system represents a mapping:"
    },
    {
     "t": "math",
     "tex": "f: \\{0, 1\\}^m \\longrightarrow \\{0, 1\\}^n"
    },
    {
     "t": "math",
     "tex": "Y_i = f_i(X_0, X_1, \\dots, X_{m-1}) \\quad \\text{for } i \\in \\{0, 1, \\dots, n-1\\}"
    },
    {
     "t": "code",
     "text": "          +-----------------------------------+\nX_0 ----->|                                   |-----> Y_0\nX_1 ----->|                                   |-----> Y_1\n  :       |   Combinational Logic Network     |   :\n  :       |   (Memoryless / No Feedback)      |   :\nX_{m-1} ->|                                   |-----> Y_{n-1}\n          +-----------------------------------+"
    },
    {
     "t": "h4",
     "text": "Core Architectural Properties:"
    },
    {
     "t": "ol",
     "items": [
      "**Memoryless Operation**: Contains **no storage elements** (no flip-flops, latches, or memory cells). Past inputs have zero influence on present outputs.",
      "**Acyclic Interconnection**: Contains **no feedback loops** from outputs to inputs. Every signal flows strictly in a forward feed direction (Direct Acyclic Graph - DAG).",
      "**Absence of Clock Excitation**: The operation is completely asynchronous; outputs update immediately after gate propagation delays elapse following an input transition.",
      "**Behavioral Contrast with Sequential Circuits**:"
     ]
    },
    {
     "t": "ul",
     "items": [
      "*Combinational*: $Y(t) = f(X(t))$",
      "*Sequential*: $Y(t) = g(X(t), Q(t))$ where $Q(t)$ is the stored present internal state vector."
     ]
    },
    {
     "t": "h3",
     "text": "1.2 Systematic Combinational Design Procedure"
    },
    {
     "t": "p",
     "text": "Every combinational block follows a deterministic, 5-stage synthesis pipeline:"
    },
    {
     "t": "code",
     "text": "[1. Word Specification] \n          \u2502\n          \u25bc\n[2. Truth Table Formulation] \n          \u2502 (Identify inputs/outputs, enumerate all 2^m combinations)\n          \u25bc\n[3. Boolean Expression Minimization]\n          \u2502 (K-Maps / Quine-McCluskey / Boolean Theorems for minimal SOP/POS)\n          \u25bc\n[4. Gate-Level Implementation]\n          \u2502 (AND-OR-NOT, All-NAND, All-NOR, or Multiplexer/Decoder structures)\n          \u25bc\n[5. Timing & Critical Path Verification]\n            (Propagation delay check, hazard elimination, fan-out check)"
    }
   ]
